        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cd17c048-eae3-537c-ab43-cd67bfe71661",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: English National Ballet, Royal Ballet\n- Places: London Coliseum, Royal Albert Hall, St. Martin's Lane, central London\n- People: Alina Cojocaru, Frank Matcham, Oswald Stoll, Fletcher Sibthorp, Darcey Bussell, Sarah Lamb, Miyako Yoshida, Joaquín Cortés, Eva Yerbabuena, Sara Baras\n- Roles: principal dancer, theatrical architect, impresario\n- Topics: dance, theatre, flamenco\n\nFacts:\n- The London Coliseum opened on 24 December 1904 as the London Coliseum Theatre of Varieties.\n- Frank Matcham designed the London Coliseum for the impresario Oswald Stoll.\n- The London Coliseum, also known as the Coliseum Theatre, is a theatre on St. Martin's Lane in central London.\n- The London Coliseum was built as one of London's largest and most luxurious family variety theatres.\n- The English National Ballet regularly performs seasons at the London Coliseum.\n- The English National Ballet has been noted for specially staged performances at the Royal Albert Hall.\n- As of November 2013, Alina Cojocaru was a principal dancer with the English National Ballet.\n- Fletcher Sibthorp painted dance figures including Royal Ballet principals Darcey Bussell, Sarah Lamb, Miyako Yoshida, and Alina Cojocaru.\n- Fletcher Sibthorp also painted flamenco performers Joaquín Cortés, Eva Yerbabuena, and Sara Baras.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
